# Anchoring: a directory pattern with no leading slash matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, not just at the repository root. That is almost never
# what these entries mean, and it bites silently -- an unanchored `media/` once
# swallowed the whole of `src/app/media/avatars/[userId]/`, so `git status`
# simply never showed the route handler that serves the volume. Everything here
# that names a root-level artifact carries a leading `/`. The exceptions are
# deliberate: `node_modules/` genuinely nests, and the Python caches below have
# to keep matching inside `old/`.

# OS-specific files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
*~

